---
/* =============================================================================
   The homepage — one implementation, two languages
   =============================================================================
   Both `/` and `/ar/` render this. The alternative — two 300-line page files —
   guarantees they drift apart, and a drifted Arabic homepage is exactly the
   "visual afterthought" §10 forbids.

   ── THE FROZEN ORDER (IA v2.0) ──────────────────────────────────────────────

     1. Hero
     2. Vibe Coding in the Real World
     3. Gear — Currently Testing
     4. Learn
     5. Playground
     6. About + Subscribe
     7. Footer                          (Base.astro)

   That order is an argument, and it runs in one direction: what I build, what
   I use to build it, what I wrote down about it, what you can try yourself,
   and who is saying all this. The two pillars lead because they are the two
   pillars; everything the reader can DO comes after everything the reader can
   READ; and the personal close is last because a close should be last.

   ── WHAT THIS REPLACED ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   The Phase 1.1 order — What I Explore · series band · Latest · Guides ·
   Prompt teaser · What I'm Building · Videos · GearNest · Newsletter · Sign-Off
   — was a LIBRARY laid out by content type. IA v2.0 lays the page out by
   pillar, so the ten strips collapse into five sections and each surface is
   reached through the one that owns it:

     Explore · Latest · Guides · Prompts · Videos → §4 Learn, and /learn
     series band                                  → §2, the featured build
     What I'm Building                            → §2 and /vibe-coding
     GearNest                                     → the footer's separate-brand
                                                     row (a separate business,
                                                     linked, never merged in)
     Newsletter + Sign-Off                        → §6, as one closing section

   Nothing was deleted. Every Phase 1.1 route is still live at exactly the URL
   it had, and the components that served those strips still serve /learn and
   the surface indexes. This page stopped being their index, that is all.

   ── EVERY SECTION COLLAPSES ON ITS OWN ──────────────────────────────────────
   §2 and §3 are gated on real assets (a build needs a real screenshot, a gear
   story needs a real photograph), §4 drops any surface with nothing published,
   §5 lists only tools you can actually open. With an empty content directory
   this page is a hero, four honest lines and a close — which is the correct
   state, not a broken one.

   CS-05: exactly one primary action on this page, and it is the hero's. Every
   other action below is secondary, ghost or a plain link.
   ========================================================================== */

import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../home/Hero.astro';
import RealWorld from '../home/RealWorld.astro';
import GearSection from '../home/GearSection.astro';
import LearnSection from '../home/LearnSection.astro';
import PlaygroundSection from '../home/PlaygroundSection.astro';
import AboutSubscribe from '../home/AboutSubscribe.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config';
import type { Lang } from '../../i18n';

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props;

const description = lang === 'ar' ? site.descriptionAr : site.description;
---

<Base lang={lang} padded={false} description={description}>
  {/* 1 — Hero. The approved implementation, unchanged. */}
  <Hero lang={lang} />

  {/* 2 — Vibe Coding in the Real World. Building with AI. */}
  <RealWorld lang={lang} />

  {/* 3 — Gear. Using and testing technology. */}
  <GearSection lang={lang} />

  {/* 4 — Learn. The gateway to the library, not the library. */}
  <LearnSection lang={lang} />

  {/* 5 — Playground. Only what you can actually open. */}
  <PlaygroundSection lang={lang} />

  {/* 6 — About + Subscribe. The close. */}
  <AboutSubscribe lang={lang} />

  {/* 7 — Footer, from Base.astro. */}
</Base>
